WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.724
Site review combines current official airspace information, permissions,

00:00:03.724 --> 00:00:08.253
asset drawings or maps, weather, lighting, terrain, obstacles, electromagnetic conditions,

00:00:08.253 --> 00:00:09.612
and ongoing operations.

00:00:09.612 --> 00:00:14.595
Coordinate with the asset owner and site-safety lead before route design.

00:00:14.595 --> 00:00:16.407
Structures create unique hazards.

00:00:16.407 --> 00:00:20.936
Wires, antennas, cranes, cables, overhangs, moving equipment, reflected navigation signals,

00:00:20.936 --> 00:00:25.013
turbulence, and radio shadowing may be hard to see.

00:00:25.013 --> 00:00:28.637
Obstacle sensing cannot replace standoff and visual awareness.

00:00:28.637 --> 00:00:33.166
Choose launch and recovery areas with stable surfaces, clear access,

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:37.243
controlled people and vehicles, reliable communication, and emergency options.

00:00:37.243 --> 00:00:42.679
Plan alternate landing areas when the route extends across a large asset.

00:00:42.679 --> 00:00:49.020
The flight path should connect overview coverage with targeted details while preserving safe distance.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:53.550
Plan camera angles, route direction, altitude strategy, turns, battery segments,

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:57.173
and areas where the aircraft must not enter.

00:00:57.173 --> 00:01:03.062
Crew roles may include pilot in command, visual observer, payload operator, site escort,

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:04.874
mission lead, and specialist.

00:01:04.874 --> 00:01:09.856
Use concise communication for hazards, asset references, collection status, battery, signal,

00:01:09.856 --> 00:01:11.215
and abort calls.

00:01:11.215 --> 00:01:15.745
Document objective, approvals, crew, aircraft, payload, conditions, route, standoff, hazards,

00:01:15.745 --> 00:01:19.369
controls, emergency actions, data handling, and abort criteria.

00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:24.804
Final go authority remains with the responsible pilot under the operating model.

00:01:24.804 --> 00:01:29.787
Deconflict with maintenance, cranes, lifts, traffic control, rail movement, energized work,

00:01:29.787 --> 00:01:31.599
deliveries, and emergency access.

00:01:31.599 --> 00:01:37.940
A route approved on a drawing may be unsafe when simultaneous site activity begins.
